          "q": "What is the most scalable way to handle environment-specific variables like Base URLs?",
          "options": [
            "Use dotenv to load environment variables and reference process.env.BASE_URL in the config's use block.",
            "Hardcode the URLs directly into every .spec.ts file.",
            "Create three separate config files (qa.config.ts, prod.config.ts) and duplicate the settings.",
            "Use a global setup file to write the URL to a text file on disk."
          ],
          "a": "Use dotenv to load environment variables and reference process.env.BASE_URL in the config's use block.",
          "explanation": "Injecting configurations via environment variables is a 12-Factor App best practice. It prevents hardcoded secrets and allows CI/CD pipelines to easily swap configurations without touching the code."
        }
      ]
