  {
    "id": "41-fundamentals-cli",
    "title": "8.2: CLI & Config Mastery",
    "url": "courses/playwright/41-fundamentals-cli",
    "group": "🧱 MODULE 8: ENTERPRISE PRACTICES",
    "level": 6,
    "weight": 15,
    "meta": {
      "time": "20 mins",
      "type": "Code",
      "outcome": "Master the Automation Skill Authority (ASA) CLI and environment variables"
    },
    "objectives": [
      {
        "id": "cli_config",
        "title": "Master .env and playwright.config.js"
      }
    ],
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "setup_env",
        "title": "Config .env",
        "hint": "Requires: 'BASE_URL' and 'API_KEY'",
        "rules": [
          {
            "type": "contains",
            "value": "BASE_URL"
          },
          {
            "type": "contains",
            "value": "API_KEY"
          },
          {
            "type": "ast_forbidden_callee",
            "value": "page.waitForTimeout"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "quizMapping": [
      {
        "objective": "cli_config",
        "weight": 100
      }
    ],
    "spec": {
      "config": ".env",
      "cli": "npx playwright"
    },
    "quizPool": {
      "Easy": [
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "scenario",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "scenario": "You are writing a new test locally and want to see the browser interactions, but your playwright.config.ts is set to headless: true by default for CI.",
          "q": "Which CLI command allows you to view the browser without modifying the configuration file?",
          "options": [
            "npx playwright test --ui",
            "npx playwright test --headed",
            "npx playwright test --show-browser",
            "npx playwright test --debug"
          ],
          "a": "npx playwright test --headed",
          "explanation": "The `--headed` flag overrides the config file to force the browser to run visibly. While `--ui` and `--debug` also show the browser, they open additional inspection tools, which might not be what you want if you just want to watch the execution run."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "code-analysis",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "code": "import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  use: {\n    baseURL: process.env.STAGING_URL,\n  }\n});",
          "q": "A Junior SDET runs tests using `npx playwright test`. The tests immediately fail because the application navigates to 'about:blank'. What is missing?",
          "options": [
            "The STAGING_URL environment variable was not set in the shell or .env file before running the tests.",
            "baseURL cannot be configured inside the 'use' block.",
            "process.env is not accessible in TypeScript config files.",
            "The defineConfig block is missing the 'projects' array."
          ],
          "a": "The STAGING_URL environment variable was not set in the shell or .env file before running the tests.",
          "explanation": "If `process.env.STAGING_URL` is undefined (because the `.env` file wasn't loaded or the variable wasn't exported in the shell), Playwright's `baseURL` becomes undefined, causing `page.goto('/')` to fail or resolve to `about:blank`."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "multi-select",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "scenario": "Your suite has 50 tests. You want to run only the tests tagged with '@smoke' on the 'Mobile Safari' project.",
          "q": "Which CLI flags must you combine to achieve this? (Select all that apply)",
          "options": [
            "--grep @smoke",
            "--project=\"Mobile Safari\"",
            "--tag @smoke",
            "--device=\"iPhone 13\"",
            "--filter @smoke"
          ],
          "a": [
            "--grep @smoke",
            "--project=\"Mobile Safari\""
          ],
          "explanation": "Playwright uses `--grep` (or `-g`) to run tests matching a specific title or tag pattern. The `--project` flag targets a specific project defined in your `playwright.config.ts`. The other flags do not exist in the standard CLI."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "scenario",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "scenario": "You pushed your code, and the GitHub Action pipeline is running. You want to ensure the pipeline stops immediately if 3 tests fail, rather than wasting 20 minutes running the rest.",
          "q": "Which configuration setting or CLI flag enforces this?",
          "options": [
            "--max-failures=3",
            "retries: 3",
            "--stop-on-failure=3",
            "fullyParallel: false"
          ],
          "a": "--max-failures=3",
          "explanation": "The `--max-failures=3` flag (or `maxFailures: 3` in the config) tells the Playwright test runner to abort the entire test suite as soon as the failure threshold is reached, saving valuable CI/CD compute minutes."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "code-analysis",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "code": "npx playwright test --workers=1",
          "q": "When diagnosing a flaky test suite that only fails in CI, why might an SDET temporarily run this command locally?",
          "options": [
            "To force tests to run sequentially to rule out parallel data collisions.",
            "To ensure the tests run on only 1 browser type.",
            "To prevent the Playwright Inspector from opening multiple windows.",
            "To reduce CPU usage on their local machine."
          ],
          "a": "To force tests to run sequentially to rule out parallel data collisions.",
          "explanation": "Setting `--workers=1` disables parallel execution. If the tests pass consistently with 1 worker but fail with 4, it strongly indicates a race condition or shared state/data collision between tests."
        }
      ],
      "Medium": [
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "code-analysis",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "code": "import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';\nimport dotenv from 'dotenv';\ndotenv.config({ path: '.env.local' });\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  use: { baseURL: process.env.BASE_URL }\n});",
          "q": "A developer commits this config. The tests pass locally, but fail instantly in the GitHub Actions pipeline. Why?",
          "options": [
            ".env.local is typically ignored by git, meaning the CI server cannot find it to load the variables.",
            "dotenv does not work in CI/CD pipelines.",
            "process.env cannot be overridden by dotenv.",
            "The path must be absolute (e.g., path.resolve('.env.local'))."
          ],
          "a": ".env.local is typically ignored by git, meaning the CI server cannot find it to load the variables.",
          "explanation": "Files like `.env.local` contain local developer secrets and are universally added to `.gitignore`. Because it is not committed to the repository, `dotenv` fails silently in CI, resulting in an undefined `BASE_URL`. CI environments should rely on injected environment variables/secrets instead of `.env` files."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "multi-select",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "scenario": "Your CI pipeline is taking 45 minutes to run. You have 3 GitHub Action runners available. You want to shard the test suite across all 3 runners.",
          "q": "Which of the following CLI commands are required on the CI runners to achieve this? (Select all that apply)",
          "options": [
            "npx playwright test --shard=1/3",
            "npx playwright test --shard=2/3",
            "npx playwright test --shard=3/3",
            "npx playwright test --parallel=3",
            "npx playwright test --split=3"
          ],
          "a": [
            "npx playwright test --shard=1/3",
            "npx playwright test --shard=2/3",
            "npx playwright test --shard=3/3"
          ],
          "explanation": "Playwright's native sharding requires passing the shard fraction to each respective CI node. Node 1 gets `--shard=1/3`, Node 2 gets `--shard=2/3`, etc. The flags `--parallel` and `--split` do not exist for sharding."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "scenario",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "scenario": "You are running tests against a staging environment that is notoriously slow today. Your locators are timing out after 30 seconds. You want to temporarily increase the timeout to 60 seconds without committing changes to the `playwright.config.ts`.",
          "q": "What is the correct way to override the test timeout from the CLI?",
          "options": [
            "npx playwright test --timeout=60000",
            "TIMEOUT=60000 npx playwright test",
            "npx playwright test --global-timeout=60000",
            "npx playwright test --wait=60000"
          ],
          "a": "npx playwright test --timeout=60000",
          "explanation": "The `--timeout` CLI flag overrides the `timeout` value set in the config file. It expects the value in milliseconds. `--global-timeout` limits the total execution time of the entire suite, not individual tests."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "code-analysis",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "code": "export default defineConfig({\n  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,\n  workers: process.env.CI ? 1 : undefined,\n});",
          "q": "What architectural intent does this configuration demonstrate?",
          "options": [
            "It optimizes for fast local development while maximizing stability and preventing parallel collisions in CI.",
            "It forces local tests to run sequentially and CI tests to run in parallel.",
            "It disables retries entirely when running on GitHub Actions.",
            "It causes the tests to run indefinitely in CI if a failure occurs."
          ],
          "a": "It optimizes for fast local development while maximizing stability and preventing parallel collisions in CI.",
          "explanation": "Locally, `process.env.CI` is false, so `retries` is 0 (fast feedback) and `workers` is undefined (uses 50% of local CPU cores for fast parallel runs). In CI, `retries` is 2 (handles flakiness) and `workers` is 1 (sequential execution to avoid resource/data collisions on underpowered CI nodes)."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "scenario",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "scenario": "A test fails in the CI pipeline. You download the HTML report, but there is no trace file available to debug the failure. Your config has `trace: 'on-first-retry'`.",
          "q": "Why is the trace file missing for this failed test?",
          "options": [
            "The test failed on its very first attempt, and retries were set to 0, so a retry never happened.",
            "Traces cannot be generated in headless mode.",
            "The HTML report does not support embedding trace files.",
            "The trace file exceeded the maximum file size limit."
          ],
          "a": "The test failed on its very first attempt, and retries were set to 0, so a retry never happened.",
          "explanation": "The `on-first-retry` setting records a trace *only* when the test fails and runs a second time (the first retry). If `retries: 0` is set in the config, a retry never triggers, so the trace is never recorded. Use `retain-on-failure` if retries are 0."
        }
      ],
      "Hard": [
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "code-analysis",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "code": "import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  globalSetup: require.resolve('./global-setup'),\n  use: {\n    baseURL: 'https://staging.app.com',\n    storageState: 'state.json',\n  },\n});",
          "q": "A test suite utilizes this config to inject an authenticated `storageState`. The `global-setup.ts` file performs an API login and writes the cookies to `state.json`. However, when you run `npx playwright test`, the first test always fails due to an outdated session, but the subsequent tests pass. What is the architectural flaw?",
          "options": [
            "Playwright loads the 'use' config before globalSetup finishes, so the first test uses an old state.json from a previous run.",
            "globalSetup cannot write files to the disk.",
            "storageState cannot be defined in the 'use' block.",
            "The API login must be performed inside a beforeEach hook, not globalSetup."
          ],
          "a": "Playwright loads the 'use' config before globalSetup finishes, so the first test uses an old state.json from a previous run.",
          "explanation": "This is a notorious race condition. If `state.json` exists from a previous run, Playwright's worker threads may read the file into memory *before* the `globalSetup` finishes overwriting it. To fix this, use project dependencies (`dependencies: ['setup']`) instead of `globalSetup`."
        },
        {
          "objective": "cli_config",
          "type": "multi-select",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "scenario": "You are managing a mono-repo. Your Playwright config is located at `packages/e2e/playwright.config.ts`, but you are currently running commands from the root directory `/`.",
