          "scenario": "You are debugging a flaky CI/CD pipeline. The pipeline runs `npm install` before executing tests. Sometimes tests fail mysteriously due to slightly different dependency versions being resolved.",
          "q": "What is the industry-standard architectural change to ensure dependencies are exactly identical to the developer's local machine?",
          "options": [
