          "a": "The container OS is missing system-level fonts.",
          "explanation": "Minimal Linux Docker images (like Ubuntu Core or Alpine) do not come with standard fonts installed. Playwright renders the DOM perfectly, but when the OS tries to paint text without font files, it renders square 'tofu' blocks. You must `apt-get install fonts-liberation` or similar."
        },
        {
          "objective": "env_validation",
          "type": "multi-select",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "scenario": "You are troubleshooting a colleague's machine. They run `git status` and see: `HEAD detached at b2a1f4c`.",
          "q": "Which of the following statements are TRUE about this specific environmental state? (Select all that apply)",
          "options": [
            "The colleague is currently looking at a specific commit rather than the tip of a branch.",
            "Any new commits made right now will not belong to any branch and may become orphaned.",
