          "a": [
            "The colleague is currently looking at a specific commit rather than the tip of a branch.",
            "Any new commits made right now will not belong to any branch and may become orphaned.",
            "The colleague can resolve this by running `git checkout main` to reattach to the main branch."
          ],
          "explanation": "A detached HEAD simply means your working directory is checked out to a specific commit hash or tag instead of a branch reference. It is perfectly safe and normal, but commits made here are easily lost unless explicitly branched. Checking out an existing branch immediately resolves it."
