            "In-Memory JavaScript Variables (Redux State)"
          ],
          "explanation": "By default, Playwright's `storageState` *only* captures Cookies and LocalStorage. It explicitly does not capture SessionStorage (which is ephemeral by definition), IndexedDB (complex storage), or raw JS memory. If your app relies on IndexedDB for auth, `storageState` will fail."
        },
        {
          "objective": "browser_context",
          "type": "scenario",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "scenario": "You want to clear the cookies in the middle of a test to simulate a session expiration.",
          "q": "Which Playwright command correctly clears the browser state?",
          "options": [
            "await context.clearCookies();",
            "await page.clear();",
            "await browser.clearCache();",
            "await page.evaluate(() => localStorage.clear());"
