            "There is no omission; Playwright handles it."
          ],
          "a": "The script fails to call `await context.close()` at the end. Manually created contexts are not automatically garbage collected like default fixtures, leading to severe memory leaks in CI.",
          "explanation": "Default fixtures (`{ page, context }`) are automatically destroyed by the Playwright Test runner. However, if you manually instantiate `browser.newContext()`, YOU are responsible for closing it. Failing to do so leaves zombie contexts hanging in memory."
        },
        {
          "objective": "browser_context",
          "type": "scenario",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "scenario": "You are testing an application that requires camera and microphone permissions. By default, Chromium prompts the user with a dialog asking for permission, which halts the headless test.",
          "q": "How do you automatically grant these permissions in Playwright?",
          "options": [
            "Click the 'Allow' button using `page.click('text=Allow')`.",
