            "`popup` captures iframes."
          ],
          "a": "There is no difference; they are aliases for the exact same underlying Context event. Playwright intercepts window creation via `window.open` or `target=\"_blank\"`.",
          "explanation": "Both events yield the exact same `Page` object. `popup` is tied specifically to the `Page` object emitting it (a child spawned from a parent), whereas `page` is emitted by the `BrowserContext`. Conceptually, they achieve the exact same goal in tab interception."
        },
        {
          "objective": "multi_tab_window",
          "type": "multi-select",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "scenario": "You are writing a test that opens 3 different tabs. You lose track of your variables.",
          "q": "How can you dynamically query the `BrowserContext` to find a specific tab based on its current URL? (Select all that apply)",
          "options": [
            "const pages = context.pages();",
            "const targetPage = pages.find(p => p.url().includes('dashboard'));",
            "const targetPage = await context.waitForEvent('url');",
