          "objective": "adv_parallel",
          "type": "mcq",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "q": "By default, how does Playwright run multiple test files (`.spec.ts`)?",
          "options": [
            "It runs them one by one (sequentially).",
            "It automatically runs the test files in parallel across multiple OS worker processes, utilizing the available CPU cores to drastically reduce execution time.",
            "It sends them to the cloud.",
            "It runs them in a single Node.js thread."
          ],
          "a": "It automatically runs the test files in parallel across multiple OS worker processes, utilizing the available CPU cores to drastically reduce execution time.",
          "explanation": "Unlike older frameworks that required complex third-party runners to achieve parallelism, Playwright's test runner is inherently parallel out of the box. Each `.spec.ts` file is assigned to an independent OS worker process."
        },
        {
          "objective": "adv_parallel",
          "type": "code-analysis",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "code": "// login.spec.ts\ntest('Login valid', async () => { ... });\ntest('Login invalid', async () => { ... });\ntest('Login empty', async () => { ... });",
          "q": "By default, how are the three tests *inside* this specific file executed relative to one another?",
          "options": [
            "In parallel.",
            "Sequentially (one after the other) in the exact order they are written. Playwright only parallelizes *files* by default, not the individual tests within a single file.",
            "Alphabetically.",
            "Randomly."
          ],
          "a": "Sequentially (one after the other) in the exact order they are written. Playwright only parallelizes *files* by default, not the individual tests within a single file.",
          "explanation": "To prevent tests that share a file from accidentally corrupting each other's state (a common issue when migrating legacy tests), Playwright guarantees sequential execution within a file unless you explicitly instruct it otherwise."
        },
        {
          "objective": "adv_parallel",
          "type": "scenario",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "scenario": "You have a massive `checkout.spec.ts` file with 20 independent tests. You want them to run simultaneously to save time.",
          "q": "How do you explicitly enable parallel execution for the tests *inside* this specific file?",
          "options": [
            "Use a `for` loop.",
            "Add `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'parallel' });` at the top of the file. This tells Playwright to spawn multiple workers and distribute the 20 tests across them, rather than running them in one worker sequentially.",
            "Pass `--workers=20` to the CLI.",
            "You cannot parallelize inside a file."
          ],
          "a": "Add `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'parallel' });` at the top of the file. This tells Playwright to spawn multiple workers and distribute the 20 tests across them, rather than running them in one worker sequentially.",
          "explanation": "You can opt-in to intra-file parallelism using `mode: 'parallel'`. However, you must guarantee that those 20 tests are completely mathematically independent. If Test 2 relies on Test 1 creating an item, `mode: 'parallel'` will instantly destroy your test suite."
