          "scenario": "You have a suite of 'Flaky' tests that rely on a 3rd-party vendor API that often drops connections.",
          "q": "Instead of using global retries, how can you explicitly instruct Playwright to retry *only* this specific fragile test block?",
          "options": [
            "Use `page.reload()`.",
            "Add `test.describe.configure({ retries: 3 })` inside the `describe` block containing those specific tests. This surgically applies retry logic only to the fragile boundaries, leaving the rest of the robust suite failing fast on 0 retries.",
            "Use a `while` loop.",
            "It is impossible."
          ],
          "a": "Add `test.describe.configure({ retries: 3 })` inside the `describe` block containing those specific tests. This surgically applies retry logic only to the fragile boundaries, leaving the rest of the robust suite failing fast on 0 retries.",
          "explanation": "Enterprise execution minimizes global configuration. If one feature is flaky, sandbox the flakiness. Overriding the global `retries` setting inside a specific block optimizes the execution graph."
        }
