          "a": "While it achieves the exact same execution result, manually pushing a 'skip' annotation and returning does not formally communicate the 'Skipped' state to Playwright's execution engine. The test will be recorded as 'Passed' (Green) in the HTML report, masking the fact that it was bypassed.",
          "explanation": "You must use the framework's semantic APIs (`test.skip`). Bypassing the engine with manual `return` statements corrupts the telemetry data. A skipped test is a Yellow warning; a manually returned test is a False Positive Green."
