          "scenario": "You want to run all tests that DO NOT have the `@flake` tag. You attempt to use a negative lookahead regex in the CLI: `npx playwright test --grep \"^(?!.*@flake).*$\"`.",
          "q": "Why is using `--grep-invert` architecturally cleaner and safer than complex Regex engines for this task?",
          "options": [
            "Regex is banned in Node.js.",
            "Negative lookaheads are computationally expensive and incredibly error-prone to escape correctly across different OS shells (Bash vs PowerShell). `--grep-invert @flake` offloads the logical inversion to Playwright's internal engine, guaranteeing absolute cross-platform execution stability.",
