          "a": "Negative lookaheads are computationally expensive and incredibly error-prone to escape correctly across different OS shells (Bash vs PowerShell). `--grep-invert @flake` offloads the logical inversion to Playwright's internal engine, guaranteeing absolute cross-platform execution stability.",
          "explanation": "Enterprise CI pipelines run on Linux, but developers work on Mac and Windows. If you use complex regex with special shell characters `!$*`, your NPM script will inevitably crash on someone's machine. Always use explicit framework flags over shell magic."
