          "a": "Because UI execution is slow. Testing 50 combinations via the browser will take 5 minutes. The UI only needs ONE test to prove the `.error` banner renders correctly. The other 49 logical combinations should be tested instantly via API or Unit tests.",
          "explanation": "This is the Ice Cream Cone anti-pattern (an inverted pyramid). If you use the browser to validate backend business logic (like password complexity rules), your test suite will inevitably collapse under its own execution weight."
