          "a": "Because it doesn't prove the system is secure; it just proves it didn't succeed perfectly. If the server crashes and returns a 500 (Internal Server Error), the test passes. You MUST explicitly assert the precise expected failure boundary: `expect(res.status()).toBe(401)` or `toBe(403)` to prove the security mechanism specifically intercepted the request.",
          "explanation": "Vague assertions hide critical bugs. An unhandled exception (500) is a major architectural failure. A 401 is an intentional architectural success. Your tests must mathematically differentiate between the two."
        },
