            "If the data seeding API fails (e.g., returns 500), the UI test will navigate to `/docs/123` and fail obscurely 10 seconds later because the document doesn't exist. Throwing a highly descriptive error immediately from the Controller acts as an architectural 'Fail-Fast' circuit breaker, saving debugging time.",
            "It slows down the test.",
            "It hides bugs."
          ],
          "a": "If the data seeding API fails (e.g., returns 500), the UI test will navigate to `/docs/123` and fail obscurely 10 seconds later because the document doesn't exist. Throwing a highly descriptive error immediately from the Controller acts as an architectural 'Fail-Fast' circuit breaker, saving debugging time.",
          "explanation": "Controllers are the guardians of data state. If they fail to establish the state, they must violently halt the test pipeline with explicit logging before the UI even attempts to launch."
        },
        {
