      "Hard": [
        {
          "objective": "data_debug",
          "type": "code-analysis",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "code": "test('Fail safely', async ({ page }) => {\n  await expect.soft(page.locator('.flaky')).toBeVisible();\n  if (test.info().errors.length > 0) return;\n  await page.click('.next-step');\n});",
          "q": "What highly advanced architectural control flow is this test implementing?",
          "options": [
            "It is a syntax error.",
            "A 'Soft-Halt' pattern. It allows the soft assertion to record the specific failure context into the Playwright report, but then explicitly aborts the test execution (`return`) to prevent the script from crashing catastrophically on `.next-step`.",
