          "a": "A 'Soft-Halt' pattern. It allows the soft assertion to record the specific failure context into the Playwright report, but then explicitly aborts the test execution (`return`) to prevent the script from crashing catastrophically on `.next-step`.",
          "explanation": "This bridges the gap between Soft and Hard assertions. You get the beautiful, highly descriptive error reporting of `expect.soft()`, but you retain the structural safety of a Hard halt to prevent chaotic downstream errors."
