          "a": "Because every `expect.soft()` call incurs asynchronous framework overhead, serializes data, and writes to the internal `testInfo` ledger. Firing 1,000 of them sequentially will take seconds. You must extract the data into an array and do a single mathematical comparison (`expect(uiArray).toEqual(baselineArray)`).",
          "explanation": "Framework APIs are not free. Calling `expect` 1,000 times inside a `for` loop is a massive architectural anti-pattern. Bulk data validation must use Bulk Array Diffing (like `toEqual`) which executes holistically in memory in 1 millisecond."
