          "a": "A mathematical, tree-like data structure that represents the physical syntax and logic of your code. Playwright builds this tree BEFORE running any tests so it understands exactly how many tests exist, what their names are, and where they are located.",
          "explanation": "Before a test can execute, the machine must read it. The AST is the 'blueprint' of your test suite. Playwright parses your `.spec.ts` files into this blueprint so its orchestrator knows how to divide the work.",
