          "a": "A strict set of automated checks (Linting, TypeScript compilation, formatting) that must pass 100% before code is allowed to be merged into the `main` branch or executed in the cloud.",
          "explanation": "Automation requires automated governance. You cannot rely on humans to spot missing `await` keywords or hardcoded `sleep` commands. The Quality Gate mathematically enforces the rules.",
