            "Major CI providers (GitHub, GitLab, Jenkins) automatically inject a global `CI=true` environment variable into the shell. Playwright's `config.ts` (and your custom code) can evaluate `process.env.CI` to dynamically alter its mathematical execution boundaries based on the host.",
            "It checks the IP address.",
            "It uses a Python script."
          ],
          "a": "Major CI providers (GitHub, GitLab, Jenkins) automatically inject a global `CI=true` environment variable into the shell. Playwright's `config.ts` (and your custom code) can evaluate `process.env.CI` to dynamically alter its mathematical execution boundaries based on the host.",
          "explanation": "Context Awareness. The framework must adapt to its environment. `process.env.CI` is the universal flag that tells the execution engine 'I am running in the cloud, be strict'."
        },
        {
          "objective": "env_mastery",
          "type": "multi-select",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "scenario": "You are building a custom Fixture that generates a uniquely named database schema for test isolation (e.g., `test_db_592`).",
          "q": "Why MUST this Fixture use `testInfo.workerIndex` combined with `process.env.CI` to name the database? (Select all that apply)",
          "options": [
            "In CI (`process.env.CI`), you must use the `workerIndex` to mathematically guarantee that 10 parallel CI workers don't try to migrate the exact same DB schema simultaneously, causing deadlocks.",
