          "a": "You can configure `bypassCSP: true` inside the `playwright.config.ts` context options. By conditionally enabling this based on `process.env.ENV === 'prod'`, Playwright instructs the Chromium engine to mathematically ignore the production server's security headers, allowing the test to execute.",
          "explanation": "E2E Architects must understand Browser Security Models. Playwright has the power to dismantle browser security rules (CSP, CORS, Ignore HTTPS Errors), but these weapons must be aggressively gated behind specific environment variables."
