          "a": "You use an external state variable (e.g., `let tokenCount = 0;`) outside the `page.route` block. Inside the interceptor, you conditionally fulfill the response based on the state variable (e.g., `if (tokenCount === 0) { ... tokenCount++; }`), essentially building a state machine inside the MITM proxy.",
          "explanation": "Advanced mocking is not just static JSON. It is mimicking the stateful behavior of a real server. The architect must program logic into the interceptor to handle dynamic authentication handshakes."
