            "Click the button really fast.",
            "Change the code."
          ],
          "a": "Use a combination of `route.fulfill` and API Fixtures. You intercept the network request sent to the Feature Flag server (e.g., `app.launchdarkly.com`) and dynamically force it to return `true` for one test run, and `false` for the second test run, giving you deterministic control over the application's A/B testing state.",
          "explanation": "Feature flags create parallel realities in production. The Automation Architect must use network interception to seize control of the flag server, allowing the test to intentionally explore every possible reality."
